ok 1 - the restore chain is two completed Slice 09 plans carrying the registered identity.revalidate transform
ok 2 - the derived chain orders both completed edges from the source schema to the active schema
ok 3 - a same-schema chain on the migrated active version is the zero-edge manifest, not an unavailable path
ok 4 - a two-edge restore applies each registered transform and appends a draft
ok 5 - every restored value is rebound to the TARGET field definition, never the source definition row
ok 6 - the restored value hashes and the payload hash are recomputed server-side across the chain
ok 7 - the immutable manifest and the verification evidence carry the ordered edges and every schema version of the chain
ok 8 - the draft records [currentDraftRevisionId, sourceRevisionId] and one outbox event and one audit record are committed
ok 9 - a replay after the entry advanced returns the first envelope with no second revision
ok 10 - a chain id that is not the derived two-edge identity is migration_chain_mismatch
ok 11 - the identity of the middle-to-active chain does not cover source to active and is refused as migration_chain_mismatch
ok 12 - an edge naming a transform the digest-verified registry cannot resolve is migration_chain_incomplete
ok 13 - a chain with an edge that is not a completed plan is migration_chain_unavailable, never guessed
ok 14 - an edge whose target version was never activated (no activation evidence) is not a registered chain edge
ok 15 - a chain edge owned by another tenant is invisible to the restoring tenant: the chain is unavailable, never disclosed
ok 16 - a source value the registered transform cannot prove against the tightened target (45 > 40) refuses the restore
ok 17 - the idempotency business hash binds the selected migration chain across a real chain
ok 18 - a same-schema restore of a revision already on the migrated active version succeeds with the zero-edge chain
ok 19 - the zero-edge restore records the empty manifest and carries the value with recomputed hashes
ok 20 - a new key with the pre-restore entry version fails the entry-version CAS across a real chain (typed VERSION_MISMATCH, P0001; cascade P2-S10-AC-025, was 40001)
ok 21 - the source revision is still an immutable snapshot on its recorded schema after the restores
ok 22 - the rolled-back probes left no restore-chain manifest in the shared chain fixture
ok 23 - restore-chain evidence records only chain identity and safe counts, never migrated values
ok
